00:52:26.540 --> 00:52:28.569
Thomas Kerber: What's the motivation behind it?

473
00:52:29.320 --> 00:52:35.970
Andrzej Kopeć: So, my understanding… Is that the motivation?

474
00:52:37.600 --> 00:52:57.599
Andrzej Kopeć: is essentially for dApps like DEXUS to be able to trace the transfers between participants easily by being guaranteed that, in some way, that tokens that are listed are by a particular API.

475
00:53:00.650 --> 00:53:03.170
Thomas Kerber: Okay, but… So…

476
00:53:06.440 --> 00:53:09.740
Thomas Kerber: I mean, that seems like a bit of a chicken and egg problem, because

477
00:53:09.900 --> 00:53:12.859
Thomas Kerber: making events as part of the API, so that

478
00:53:13.110 --> 00:53:17.460
Thomas Kerber: you can make sure that they are as satisfying an API feels

479
00:53:19.590 --> 00:53:27.040
Thomas Kerber: I guess what's not clear to me is, does the calling contract Actually need to…

480
00:53:28.190 --> 00:53:37.809
Thomas Kerber: Intercept and understand the events, or is it just that they want to make sure that those events get emitted to something external?

481
00:53:38.560 --> 00:53:39.709
Andrzej Kopeć: That's the latter.

482
00:53:40.670 --> 00:53:41.330
Thomas Kerber: Okay.

